<title>FRANCE: Air France Paris cargo tonnage share dips.</title>
<headline>Air France Paris cargo tonnage share dips.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France's share of global air cargo tonnage handled at the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in January 1997 decreased on the 1996 as a whole figure, Aeroport de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Air France's share of ADP's global cargo tonnage in the month in question, totalling 81,925 tonnes, was 52.7 percent compared to 55.5 percent in calendar 1996.</p>
<p>In second place was Federal Express, which increased its share from 6.8 percent for calendar 1996 to 7.8 percent in January 1997.</p>
<p>The top 10 cargo-handling airlines at the ADP, by tonnage share, in January 1997, together with 1996 full-year tonnage share, were as follows:</p>
<p>			    Jan 97	   1996</p>
<p> Air France	     52.7pct	 55.5pct</p>
<p> FedEx		     7.8	     6.8</p>
<p> Air France Europe     3.4	     3.8</p>
<p> American Airlines     2.2	     2.0</p>
<p> Air Canada		2.2	     1.7</p>
<p> L'Aeropostale	   2.0	     1.9</p>
<p> Japan Airlines	  1.8	     1.6</p>
<p> Air Jet		   1.7	     1.3</p>
<p> Cathay Pacific	  1.6	     1.8</p>
<p> United Airlines	 1.6	     1.3</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
